        <fig id="article-26430.image.f3" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Stahl Ear Deformity. Note the third, superoposteriorly directed crus of the antihelix. The presence of this supernumerary crus causes the superoposterior aspect of the helical rim to flatten. Contributed by MH Hohman, MD, FACS</p>
          </caption>
